.TH SDL_ELF_NOTE_DLOPEN 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ELF_NOTE_DLOPEN \- Add a note that your application has dynamic shared library dependencies.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_dlopennote.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_ELF_NOTE_DLOPEN(feature, description, priority, ...) \(rs
.BI "    SDL_ELF_NOTE_INTERNAL(                                       \(rs
.BI "        \(dq[{\(rs\(dqfeature\(rs\(dq:\(rs\(dq\(dq feature                               \(rs
.BI "        \(dq\(rs\(dq,\(rs\(dqdescription\(rs\(dq:\(rs\(dq\(dq description                      \(rs
.BI "        \(dq\(rs\(dq,\(rs\(dqpriority\(rs\(dq:\(rs\(dq\(dq priority                            \(rs
.BI "        \(dq\(rs\(dq,\(rs\(dqsoname\(rs\(dq:\(dq SDL_DLNOTE_JSON_ARRAY(__VA_ARGS__) \(dq}]\(dq,   \(rs
.BI "        SDL_DLNOTE_UNIQUE_NAME);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
You can do this by adding the following to the global scope:

.IP
.EX
SDL_ELF_NOTE_DLOPEN(
    "png",
    "Support for loading PNG images using libpng (required for APNG)",
    SDL_ELF_NOTE_DLOPEN_PRIORITY_RECOMMENDED,
    "libpng12.so.0"
)
.EE
.PP

A trailing semicolon is not needed\[char46]
.PP
Or if you support multiple versions of a library, you can list them:

.IP
.EX
// Our app supports SDL1, SDL2, and SDL3 by dynamically loading them
SDL_ELF_NOTE_DLOPEN(
    "SDL",
    "Create windows through SDL video backend",
    SDL_ELF_NOTE_DLOPEN_PRIORITY_REQUIRED
    "libSDL-1.2.so.0", "libSDL2-2.0.so.0", "libSDL3.so.0"
)
.EE
.PP

This macro is not available for compilers that do not support variadic macro\(aqs\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

